<section class="case-summary"><div><p class="eyebrow">The problem</p><h2>A falling metric had several plausible explanations—and no single view showed the whole system.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>This self-initiated example follows a customer-satisfaction scenario from performance decline through intervention and recovery. It is designed for contexts where results, decisions and external pressures are being interpreted differently by different people.</p><p>Instead of forcing every question into one complex diagram, the sequence gives each visual tool a distinct job.</p></div></section>

<section class="decision-band"><span>02</span><div><p class="eyebrow">The decision</p><h2>Move from the most accessible view to the deepest one.</h2></div></section>

<section class="case-gallery">
  <figure class="gallery-wide"><img src="/img/Linea/behaviour-over-time-chart-performance.webp" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Behaviour-over-time chart with annotated events."><figcaption><strong>What happened?</strong> The timeline makes performance and surrounding events visible without overclaiming cause.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/Linea/systems-analysis-crisis-diagnostic-framework-timeline.webp" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Four-phase diagnostic timeline."><figcaption><strong>How did the situation unfold?</strong> A phase model gives the audience a shared chronology.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/Linea/change-management-lag-time-framework-infographic.webp" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Decision and action timeline showing delays before results."><figcaption><strong>Why were results delayed?</strong> Separate decision and action lines show that work was underway before the metric recovered.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/Linea/stacked-dashboard-data-narrative-presentation-slide.webp" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Stacked dashboard showing performance and operational pressures."><figcaption><strong>What else was changing?</strong> Aligned measures provide context without creating a conventional dashboard.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure><img src="/img/Linea/causal-loop-diagram-systems-thinking-presentation-slide.webp" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Causal loop map explaining decline and recovery."><figcaption><strong>How did the parts interact?</strong> A causal loop map replaces a single-cause story with a system explanation.</figcaption></figure>
</section>

<section class="case-outcome"><div><p class="eyebrow">The practical output</p><h2>A presentation sequence that supports both general and specialist conversations.</h2></div><p>This is self-initiated work, created to demonstrate our <a href="/services/information-design/">information design</a> approach to structure and mechanism. Simpler views can stand alone; the causal model is available when a guided, deeper discussion is needed.</p></section>

